@startuml
title Centralized & Declarative Logging Architecture

package "Spring Boot Application" {
  
  [Kafka Consumer] --> [Transformation Engine]
  [Transformation Engine] --> [Vendor API Client Decorator]
  [Vendor API Client Decorator] --> [Vendor API (via API Gateway)]

  ' AOP interceptors cross-cut services
  component "AOP Logging Interceptor" as AOP
  AOP ..> [Kafka Consumer] : logs entry/exit, timing
  AOP ..> [Transformation Engine] : logs transformation metadata
  AOP ..> [Vendor API Client Decorator] : logs retry attempts

  ' Decorator wraps external API calls
  component "Vendor API Client Decorator" as Decorator
  Decorator --> [Vendor API (via API Gateway)]

  ' MDC enriches all logs
  component "MDC Context" as MDC
  MDC ..> AOP : traceId, vendor, eventType
  MDC ..> Decorator : retryCount, status
  MDC ..> [Kafka Consumer] : topic, partition, offset

  ' Logging infrastructure
  component "SLF4J API" as SLF4J
  component "Logback Impl" as Logback
  component "Async Appender" as AsyncAppender
  component "JSON Encoder (Logstash)" as Encoder
  component "Splunk / File Sink" as Splunk

  [Kafka Consumer] --> SLF4J
  [Transformation Engine] --> SLF4J
  [Vendor API Client Decorator] --> SLF4J
  AOP --> SLF4J

  SLF4J --> Logback
  Logback --> AsyncAppender
  AsyncAppender --> Encoder
  Encoder --> Splunk
}

' External system
[Vendor API (via API Gateway)] as API

@enduml
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

How to Read This Diagram

AOP Interceptor: Cross-cuts service layers (consumer, transformer, vendor client). Handles entry/exit logs, timings, exceptions.

Vendor API Decorator: Wraps outbound API calls → logs retries, HTTP statuses, and enriches logs with vendor context.

MDC Context: Populates log entries with traceId, spanId, vendor, eventType, etc. Automatically included in every log line.

SLF4J + Logback: Standard logging stack.

Async Appender: Buffers and writes logs asynchronously (debug/audit).

JSON Encoder: Formats logs into structured JSON for Splunk ingestion.

Splunk Sink: Final log destination (files shipped to Splunk, or direct stream).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This visual shows where each logging concern lives in the architecture:

Cross-cutting (AOP),

API wrapper (Decorator),

Context propagation (MDC),

Infrastructure (Async + JSON + Splunk).

