@startuml
title Simplified Centralized Logging in Main + Resubmission Flow

package "Event Processing" {
  [Kafka Consumer] --> [Transformation Engine]
  [Transformation Engine] --> [Vendor API Client]
}

package "Resubmission Flow" {
  [Resubmission Scheduler] --> [Transformation Engine]
  [Transformation Engine] --> [Vendor API Client]
}

' Cross-cutting Logging
rectangle "AOP Logging Interceptors" as AOP
rectangle "MDC Context (traceId, vendor, eventType, retryCount)" as MDC
rectangle "Vendor API Decorator (logs retries, errors)" as Decorator

AOP ..> [Kafka Consumer]
AOP ..> [Resubmission Scheduler]
AOP ..> [Transformation Engine]

Decorator ..> [Vendor API Client]
MDC ..> AOP
MDC ..> Decorator

' Logging Infrastructure
[Application Code] --> [SLF4J API]
[SLF4J API] --> [Logback]
[Logback] --> [Async Appender (DEBUG/AUDIT)]
[Logback] --> [Sync Appender (ERROR/CRITICAL)]
[Async Appender (DEBUG/AUDIT)] --> [JSON Encoder]
[Sync Appender (ERROR/CRITICAL)] --> [JSON Encoder]
[JSON Encoder] --> [Log Files / Splunk]

@enduml
------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Main & Resubmission Flows

Main Flow:

Kafka Consumer → Transformation Engine → Vendor API Client.

Resubmission Flow:

Resubmission Scheduler → Transformation Engine → Vendor API Client.

Both flows pass through the same logging infrastructure.

2. Cross-Cutting Logging

AOP Logging Interceptors:

Automatically log method entry/exit, execution time, and exceptions.

Works for both main consumer and resubmission scheduler.

MDC Context:

Injects extra info into every log line (traceId, vendor, eventType, retryCount).

Helps correlate logs across distributed systems (Kafka + Vendor API).

Vendor API Decorator:

Wraps API client calls.

Logs retries, HTTP status codes, errors.

Keeps business logic clean.

3. Logging Infrastructure

SLF4J API: Facade for logging. Application only calls logger.info(...) etc.

Logback: The actual logging engine.

Async Appender: Handles DEBUG/AUDIT logs asynchronously so performance isn’t impacted.

Sync Appender: Handles ERROR/CRITICAL logs synchronously, ensuring no important errors are lost.

JSON Encoder: Formats logs into structured JSON with MDC fields.

Log Files / Splunk: Logs are written locally and shipped to Splunk for searching, dashboards, and alerting.
